# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Fei Shuang et al. (2026). Benchmarking chemically scalable machine-learning interatomic potentials for large-scale simulations of multicomponent alloys.
#   Physical Review Materials. doi:10.1103/1qc9-ypyb  arXiv:2604.01642v3
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2604.01642v3 (sha256 58e732484866d56a...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 293 (Dataset/benchmark). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/shuang2026.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: the published UNEP-v1 NEP4 model and the GRACE-FS-S/M/L
# and GRACE-2L models trained here on the UNEP-v1 data set of 16 metals and
# their binary alloys, with training and test energy, force and stress
# MAEs and RMSEs (Tables I and II), the training cost of GRACE-FS-M (Fig.
# 1d) and the stated inference speeds (Fig. 3). Ensemble averages (Table
# III), uncertainty correlations, MD energy drift and the spall simulations
# are not encoded.

