###############################################################################
# Q11 -- Computational resources
###############################################################################

# GRACE-FS-M trained on one A100 within one day (24 GPU hours, Fig. 1d);
# UNEP-v1 had needed ten days on four A100 GPUs (960 GPU hours) in its
# original training. Inference (Fig. 3): UNEP-v1 29.4 (H100) and 15.4
# (A100) Matom-step/s for 2.05 million Cu atoms, 19.7 and 10.6 for the HEA
# at 256 thousand atoms; GRACE-FS-M 0.503 (Cu) and 0.571 (HEA) Matom-step/s
# on 192 CPU cores and about 0.73-0.78 on H100 (range not encoded). Per-atom
# times are 1/speed.

###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - The quoted Cu speed of 29.4 Matom-step/s is stated at 2.05 million atoms; the A100 and CPU Cu values are 'at the same system size'. The HEA CPU value is stated without a system size and is attached to the 256-thousand-atom case of the same paragraph (Fig. 3b).
# - UNEP-v1 is the model of song2024 (not retrained here); it is a paper-local run. Ensemble-averaged errors (Table III), Spearman correlations of uncertainty, energy drift and spall strengths are not encoded.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).
# - Evaluation roles and data, base models, inference timings with their system sizes, and the source location of each value are recorded in the encoding input (artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/shuang2026.yaml) until the schema has terms for them.

